<h4 dir=3D"auto" data-sourcepos=3D"68:1-68:18">
<a id=3D"user-content-main-concepts" class=3D"anchor" aria-hidden=3D"true" =
href=3D"https://git.epam.com/epmc-acm-public/aws-associate-training/-/tree/=
master/materials/provisioning_services#main-concepts"></a>Main concepts</h4=
>
<p dir=3D"auto" data-sourcepos=3D"69:1-71:347">Cloudformation operates with=
 templates and stacks. Template contains all the resources you want to be c=
reated using JSON or YAML formatted text.
Stack is a logical unit of related resources. You create, update, and delet=
e a collection of resources by creating, updating, and deleting stacks.
If you need to make changes to the running resources in a stack, you update=
 the stack. Before making changes to your resources, you can generate a cha=
nge set, which is a summary of your proposed changes. Change sets allow you=
 to see how your changes might impact your running resources, especially fo=
r critical resources, before implementing them.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto" data-sourcepos=3D"73:1-73:87"><a rel=3D"nofollow noreferrer=
 noopener" href=3D"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/Use=
rGuide/cfn-whatis-concepts.html" target=3D"_blank">https://docs.aws.amazon.=
com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/cfn-whatis-concepts.html</a></p>
